      "nets": ["VCC", "GND"],
      "observed": "On sheet /DISPLAY/, BS0 is tied to VCC, while BS1 and BS2 are tied to GND. This straps the SSD1306 for a different interface mode than the intended I2C mode.",
      "expected": "The specification requires BS0→GND, BS1→VCC, and BS2→GND for I2C mode.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "U3 BS0 (pin 10) → VCC; BS1 (pin 11) → GND; BS2 (pin 12) → GND (sheet /DISPLAY/, page 3)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "BS0 (pin 10) → GND; BS1 (pin 11) → VCC; BS2 (pin 12) → GND"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The display is strapped out of I2C mode, so the MCU's two-wire display signals are unlikely to communicate with it.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The display interface-select pins are strapped differently from the specified I2C configuration: BS0 and BS1 are reversed. The SSD1306 is therefore likely to select a non-I2C mode."
}

